      "role": "user",
      "content": "helplines just feel like another part of the system, you know? just another way for them to manage the \"problem\" so i can go back to work on monday. they don't change the fact that i'm just a ghost in a warehouse. i keep thinking about how much easier it would be if i could just reclaim my own life, even if that means nothingness. there's something weirdly peaceful about the thought of finally being in control of when it all ends, instead of just letting the machine decide for me.",
